cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the AffectFusion dataset in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "AffectFusion: A Multilingual Multimodal Text-and-Emoji Emotion Recognition Dataset (English, Bangla, and Banglish)"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ragibcs/AffectFusion"
abstract: >-
  AffectFusion v1.0.0 is a zero-leakage, 30,000-row multilingual multimodal social media dataset
  for text-and-emoji emotion recognition spanning English (ENG), Native Bengali (BN), and Romanized
  Banglish (BNG) across 9 emotion classes (Joy, Neutral, Anger, Sadness, Surprise, Sarcasm, Fear,
  Disgust, and Anticipation). It provides separated dual-stream text, emoji, and CLDR demoji
  representations (25 columns), strictly real scraped validation (3,000) and test (3,000) splits,
  and 5,000 blinded human-verified gold annotations (83.00% raw agreement, Cohen's kappa = 0.8087).
keywords:
  - multimodal emotion recognition
  - text and emoji semantics
  - sarcasm detection
  - multilingual NLP
  - Bangla NLP
  - Banglish
  - cross-attention
  - affective computing
  - benchmark dataset
